## Security and authority

- no teen, journal, voice, media, parent, credential, or applicant-private content;
- no client grants on the economic intelligence tables;
- no automatic application, funding, approval, merge, deployment, or external communication;
- city staff and program owners remain authoritative for local law and eligibility;
- no approval carries forward between migration, integration, deployment, and rollback.

## Required gates before integration

- exact-head repository typecheck;
- Economic Intelligence Playwright workflow with real steps and logs;
- rollback-only migration validation;
- Supabase security/performance advisors after application;
- separate founder integration approval.

## Remaining production proof

- apply the migration only after required evidence;
- deploy the API only after integration and deployment gates;
- onboard a second live jurisdiction without adding city-specific code;
- record post-deploy runtime and database-backed portability evidence.
